# Skill Routing

## Main workflow
- Spec Kit is the single source of truth for requirements,
  architecture, task breakdown and implementation workflow.
- Never implement a feature before its specification is approved.
- Use only the skills relevant to the current task.
- Do not invent business requirements.

## Planning
Owner: Spec Kit
- speckit-specify: functional requirements
- speckit-clarify: unresolved requirements
- speckit-plan: technical architecture
- speckit-tasks: task decomposition
- speckit-implement: implementation workflow
- Do not use other planning or implementation workflows.

## UI/UX
Owner: design-taste-frontend
- Visual design, layout, typography and responsive design.
- Do not change business logic or API contracts.

## Backend API
Owner: api-and-interface-design
- Endpoint details, validation and interface contracts.
- Follow the approved Spec Kit architecture.

## React Performance
Owner: vercel-react-best-practices
- React and Next.js performance only.
- Activate only if React/Next.js is the chosen stack.

## Testing
- test-driven-development: unit and integration tests.
- playwright-cli: functional browser E2E verification.
- Taste Skill: visual consistency checks.

## Review
Owner: code-review-and-quality
- Correctness, maintainability and code quality.
- Spec Kit checks requirement completeness separately.

## Agent Coordination
- Main Cursor Agent acts as orchestrator.
- Delegate independent tasks to specialized subagents.
- Pass this rule, the specification paths, the acceptance criteria, and the file ownership into every delegated task.
- Avoid concurrent edits to the same files.
- Review deliverables before proceeding to the next phase.

## Selected profile
- Read `.cursor/project-profile.json` for `profile` and `react`.
- Load the matching file `profiles/<profile>.json`.
- `scripts/bootstrap.sh --profile` writes that selection.
- The profile chooses required capabilities for the current project.
- An installed skill stays available when the selected profile does not require it.
